It's been awhile since I actually pushed anything out; I've been caught 
up in some stuff at work, and there's only so much time in any given
day that I can bring myself to sit down and write code.  But things are
starting to slow down, so hopefully I can bend some more things around
now.

I've noticed that the majority of the stuff I have left on my "ideas"
list requires a savebreak to properly implement, so you can expect one
coming soon, either on the 24th or the 2nd.  This will help clean up
some of the stuff that's remaining.

Other than that, the change list will mostly speak for itself; enjoy.
The Windows binaries are updated and ready to go.

Changelog so far...

2/17:

	DR: Kicking non-large monsters who are standing in front of a pit 
		 may have an amusing result
	DR: Weapon probabilities juggled; most polearms set to '0' (will be 
		 removed on a future savebreak, but for now this keeps them out 
		 of the 'random' pile)
	DR: New toy: the wand of wind.  Does what it says on the tin.
	DR: Windows binaries updated.

2/16:  Obvious two-week vacation.  :D

	DR: Bug fix: rust traps won't rot leather armor anymore
	DR: Bug fix: monsters who change level while you're targeting with 
		 a polearm will no longer mess up the polearm targeting routines
	DR: Many potions now have a lesser effect when diluted.
	DR: Healing and extra healing potions now heal more HP.
	DR: Helm of opposite alignment now adjusts your alignment record when 
		 put on and removed.
		 - Your past actions are taken into account by your new god.  If 
		 you've been nothing but Lawful, a Chaotic god is going to need to 
		 see you do some chaotic things before suddenly putting you in his 
		 good graces.
		 - By the same token, if you immediately take the helm off and revert 
		 to Lawful, your past actions will still largely appeal to your god, 
		 though you get a penalty for conversion.
		 - This probably matches up with vanilla change C343-343, though I 
		 can't say for sure.
	DR: New description of alignment level beyond "transgressed" in 
		 enlightenment effect/endgame dumps.
	DR: Offering the Amulet of Yendor with negative alignment is no longer 
		 a good thing.

2/2:

	DR: erode_obj() rewritten to better support all damage types; this fixes 
		 some odd messages with 'destroy armor' and lays a foundation for 
		 having _all_ object damage be routed through erode_obj().
	DR: Bug fix: whining about "couldn't place lregion" on Fire plane fixed
	DR: Rodney now has an AT_WEAP attack in addition to his AT_CLAW so he can 
		 wield weapons
	DR: "Hungry" shows up slightly earlier on the nutrition scale; "Weak" 
		 unchanged.  (the practical effect of this is some extra warning that 
		 you're getting hungry and should go looking for bodies.)

